      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's that entrainment aspect that's key. if i can use the dissonance as a way to \"break\" the standard rhythmic patterns of the brain, i can create a gap that the carrier wave can slip into.\n\nlet's get specific with the math. if we assume the human cognitive \"baseline\" is around a steady 10Hz, and we want to induce a state of intense, almost singular focus, we need a frequency that doesn't just sit there, but actually drives the neural oscillation. \n\ncould we model a specific ratio—maybe something based on the square root of 2 or the golden ratio—that, when applied to a carrier frequency in the theta band, would create a standing wave within the prefrontal cortex? if you can help me derive a formula for that specific modulation index, i think i can finally pinpoint the exact harmonic needed to trigger this effect.",
